fact WorkItem(id: "WI-590", description: some(value: "Finiteness Phase D (proposal library/003, OPTIONAL cleanup): replace the separate finite combinator carriers (FiniteMappedStream/FiniteFilteredStream) with conditional-instance reuse of the single mapped/filtered carrier — 'a mapped stream is finite when its source is finite' via the witness-sort + requires pattern (EqList precedent). Requires parameterizing the mapped carrier over its SOURCE SORT so the field type preserves finiteness (today source: Stream erases it). Pure cleanup, no capability change. Depends on Phase C."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-589", "WI-599"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Claimed(agent: "claude", since: "2026-06-30T19:05:09Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-590", name: "typing")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-590", author: "claude", content: "Gap C root-caused (the remaining blocker for the recursive-collect compaction): a self-receiver op's return tail does NOT thread its type params when invoked on an abstract receiver. In the witness collect drain, `splitFirst(m)` (m : TestMapped[Source=S, Src=Src, T=T, ...] — the witness's own abstract op params) returns a destructured `rest` whose inferred type is a bare `Var` (Rigid/Global), NOT `TestMapped[T=T,...]`. Traced: carrier_param_receiver bails at `sort_functor_of_view(rest) == None` because rest is a Var, so bind_spec_params_from_carrier_param is never called and FiniteCollection.collect(rest)'s Element stays ?_  → 'expected List[T=?T], got List[T=?_]'. The CONCRETE dispatch threads fine (Element←Int64); only the abstract/recursive case fails. NOT authoring-fixable: declaring splitFirst's param explicitly parameterized (TestMapped[Source=Source,...] instead of bare TestMapped) does NOT help. Candidate fix lives in the WI-357/WI-393 carrier-grounding family (e.g. an identity self-provision view when carrier_sym == spec_sort, so a self-receiver op grounds its sort params directly from the receiver's type args). This is squarely WI-599's scope (it already names 'ground a body-less collect() on an abstract FiniteCollection field'). The recursion-FREE drain alternative is blocked by WI-605 (inline lambda in op body).", at: "2026-06-30T19:58:18Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-590", author: "claude", content: "Design (A) VERIFIED sound + executable plan (decision: map/filter return FiniteCollection, not FiniteStream — the single carrier can only provide the CARRIER-PARAM spec FiniteCollection via a witness; FiniteStream is self-receiver and CANNOT be witnessed, confirmed by probe). Soundness verified by probe: FiniteCollection.collect(mk(finiteList, f)) type-checks; FiniteCollection.collect(mk(infiniteNats, f)) is REJECTED ('no impl matches') — the witness's requires FiniteCollection[C=Source] gate makes a mapped stream finite IFF its source is. EXECUTABLE PLAN: (1) combinators.anthill — parameterize MappedStream & FilteredStream over a new 'sort Source = ?' param; field becomes source: Source (was Stream[Src,ES]); splitFirst return tail explicitly threaded MappedStream[Source=Source,Src=Src,T=T,ES=ES,EF=EF]; body uses QUALIFIED Stream.splitFirst(src) (src:Source abstract). provides Stream stays unconditional. (2) finite_combinators.anthill — REPLACE FiniteMappedStream/FiniteFilteredStream with WITNESS sorts MappedStreamFinite/FilteredStreamFinite: requires FiniteCollection[C=S,Element=Src,E=ES]; fact FiniteCollection[C=MappedStream[Source=S,...],Element=T,E={ES,EF}]; operation collect drain using QUALIFIED MappedStream.splitFirst(m) (gap C / WI-606 workaround — UNqualified leaves rest:?_). (3) finite_collection.anthill — map/filter construct mapped(c,f)/filtered(c,p) (Source=C), return FiniteCollection[C=MappedStream[...],...] (or bare carrier); drop fmapped/ffiltered imports; finiteIterator can stay (unused by map now) or be removed per WI-599. (4) Validate DISPATCH COHERENCE: xs.map(inc).size() must still pick FiniteCollection.map (List provides FiniteCollection depth 1) over Iterable.map (depth 2) — the probes did NOT test competing maps; wi492/wi278/wi439/wi588/eval_test behavioral assertions are the oracle (their carrier-name mentions are COMMENTS only, update for accuracy). (5) embedded list rustland/anthill-stl/src/stdlib.rs keeps finite_combinators entry (file repurposed). Two delivered typer fixes (provider-requires base-sort + EffectsRuntime dispatch skip, commit 3ccc19d1) are PREREQS that make the witness load+dispatch.", at: "2026-06-30T20:31:52Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-590", author: "claude", content: "RESIDUAL RISK for the rewrite (not cheaply de-riskable in a standalone probe): the CHAINING xs.map(f).size() / map.map.collect under the single carrier depends on (a) dispatch coherence — FiniteCollection.map must still win over Iterable.map on a finite receiver (List depth 1 vs 2; should hold, provision graph unchanged) — and (b) EFFECT-ROW closure through the chained map (a standalone probe leaked an undeclared  effect; in the REAL FiniteCollection.map the access row E + transform row EffP bind from the carrier provision + the f-arrow, the WI-594 mechanism that already works for the CURRENT FiniteStream-returning map). Both are only validatable by doing the actual stdlib rewrite and running wi492/wi278/wi439/wi588/eval_test as the oracle — if effect closure breaks, it is the WI-594/599 family. CORE design (witness load+dispatch, qualified-splitFirst collect drain, finite-iff-source soundness gate) is VERIFIED. Map RETURN TYPE: bare carrier MappedStream[Source=C,...] dispatches FiniteCollection.size/collect/map on the result via the witness (chaining resolves; the leak was effects only).", at: "2026-06-30T20:34:23Z")
